@startuml retention-v2-depth-memo
' ============================================================================
' Why the V2 reader memoizes counts on (digest, remaining key width) and not
' on the digest alone (task 7925): the store misplaced_shared_leaf_store of
' formal/rocq/stack_safe_pda/theories/RetentionV2Format.v (theorem 19), whose
' leaf node 2 is reachable at two different widths.
'   BLUE   #1565C0  inner radix nodes
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  a leaf reached where its prefix fills the remaining width
'   RED    #C62828  the same leaf reached where its prefix does not fit
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  what each memo decides
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ObjectBorderColor #455A64
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64

title <b>Why the count memo is keyed by (digest, width)</b>\none leaf object reached at two widths: it fits at one and not at the other

object "root (node 1)" as root #BBDEFB {
  inner node, empty prefix
  reached at width 48
}
object "node 3" as inner #BBDEFB {
  inner node, empty prefix
  reached at width 47
}
object "node 2" as shared #C8E6C9 {
  leaf, 47-byte prefix
  at width 47: fits, counts 1
  at width 46: does not fit
}
object "node 4" as last #C8E6C9 {
  leaf, 46-byte prefix
  reached at width 46: fits
}

root --> shared : <color:#2E7D32>edge 0, width 47</color>
root --> inner : edge 1, width 47
inner --> shared : <color:#C62828>edge 0, width 46</color>
inner --> last : edge 1, width 46

note right of inner #FFF3E0
  <b>Digest-only memo</b> (the mutant of theorem 19):
  node 2 was counted 1 at width 47, so its digest
  hits the memo at width 46 and the shape is never
  checked again. Total 1 + (1 + 1) = 3: accepted.
  ----
  <b>(digest, width) memo</b> (the reader, theorem 18):
  (node 2, 46) is a new key, so the shape check runs
  and refuses EndpointDepth with remaining 46 and
  prefix 47. Node 4 is never read.
end note
@enduml
